de things  like trouble and terror  town where a group of players have to  work out which one among them is the  traitor trying to kill everyone off and  a bizarre elevator riding simulator  called elevator sauce where each floor  offers increasingly dumb experiences  it's worth noting that garrysmod and  Black Mesa dirt even scratched the  surface of all the great half-life mods  cry of fear natural selection and the  Stanley parable are all honorable  mentions in that category there's  another game that fits within that  half-life mods list but it's just a  little too impressive to be constrained  to an honorable mention and that's  counter-strike this popular team-based  multiplayer half-life mod featured  hostage rescue and bomb defusal missions  with each team equipped with unique  equipment and goals and basically gamers  lapped it up like dota counter-strike  offered up a super-fun multiplayer  experience that featured an emphasis on  teamwork and effective communication  required for victory and as seems to  have become a theme with the company  valve proved they knew a good thing when  they saw it the company snapped up the  mods creators and gave them jobs at  valve they then contributed to the  eventual creation of CS sauce and CS  global Offensive let me know which mod  is your favorite and what you think of  the modding community either in that  comment section down below or you can  find me on Twitter where I'm at chest  MacDonald I'll catch you again next week  [Music]

